    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1181">

                <pb facs="1123" n="1111" sameAs="frus:frus1943v04/pg1111"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.24/842: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Turkey</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Ankara</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-12-31T20:00:00+02:00">December 31,
                            1943—8 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received January 1, 1944—10:34 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2122. In conversation with the Minister for Foreign Affairs last night
                    (Department’s 792, September 30, Embassy’s 1806, November 4, Department’s 980,
                    December 28 [<hi rendition="#italic">29</hi>])<anchor n="1" xml:id="d1181-f1"/>
                    I urged him to expedite his reply to our most recent proposal in connection with
                    the master Lend-Lease agreement and stressed the desirability of concluding the
                    agreement as soon as possible. Numan said he had been delayed in making his
                    reply to us by a desire to study the British proposals in connection with our
                    agreement. He added that he expected to be in a position shortly after the first
                    of the year to conclude an agreement with us and indicated that he did not
                    anticipate any difficulties.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Steinhardt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d1181-f1" n="1" xml:id="d1181-f1-content">
                <p>Telegrams No. 1806 and No. 980 not printed; in telegram No. 980 (867.24/807) the
                    Department had requested the Ambassador to ascertain the Turkish reaction to the
                    proposal advanced in telegram No. 792.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
